WEBVTT

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:33.490
Eh?

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:35.600
Oh?

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.430
Takagi-san, you're still wearing your summer uniform.

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:42.500
That said, you've changed into your winter uniform.

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:44.330
CHANGING UNIFORMS

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:45.210
Changing uniforms.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:50.830
That's because the forecast said it'll be cold today.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:54.300
Eh? You watched the forecast.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.320
I was careless.

00:01:57.430 --> 00:01:59.630
We did say if we change into winter uniforms together,

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:01.600
it's my win, right?

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:02.760
Did we?

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:05.080
Alright, I'll let you win this one.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:07.130
Wait, that's not what I want.

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:12.660
But competing and admitting defeat like that,

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:14.630
you're really careless.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:18.000
Besides, you're still wearing summer uniform
in such cold weather.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.860
But I don't think it's cold.

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:23.130
You're still trying to act strong.

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:27.250
All right. I win if you say

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.200
the word "samui" (cold).

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:33.130
You can change that to "if I admit it's cold", you know.

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:34.960
What's the difference?

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.100
Who knows?

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:41.930
All right. I'm in for this.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:42.860
Okay.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.860
Though it's irrelevant to our topic,

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.530
anyone interested in the history of kanji...

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:54.860
Papa said he saw a UFO again.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:57.330
Look carefully.

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:58.260
Yes.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:00.700
Remember to show it to your parents.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:10.130
I've tried not to be obvious that

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:13.060
I want to bait her to say the word "cold" for the whole day.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.060
Therefore, Takagi-san

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:18.600
must think I'd forgotten about the competition.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.360
This is my chance!

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:23.400
Takagi-san.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:25.700
It's a bit of a sudden but I want to ask you a question.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.630
Ben runs faster than Bob,

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:30.260
but runs slower than Sam.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:32.230
If the three of them race together,

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:33.600
who will lose?

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:34.800
Bob?

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:35.800
That's correct.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:38.130
Then, how about Sam?

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:41.830
The answer is "ichi" (number one).

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:44.100
If you link them together,

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.100
Sam "ichi".

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:47.760
"Samu-ichi"!

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.700
"Samui-chi" (cold)!

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.100
You lose if you say "itai" (ouch).

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:57.530
How do you say that word again, not massage...

00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:59.000
"Seitai" (rub massage)?

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:00.030
Nishikata, you've lost.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.700
Se... itai!

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:06.800
I will have my revenge!

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.930
Takagi-san,

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.580
say it now!

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:11.860
Let me see,

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:13.080
Sam is...

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:16.260
Number one.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:20.100
How did this happen?

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.260
Am I right?

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:22.960
Yes.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.100
What a pity.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:29.130
You wanted to trick me into saying it, right?

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:34.030
I've run out of ideas.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:38.130
Hold on, there's still a chance.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.630
The prerequisite for Takagi-san to be calm...

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:41.460
That is...

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:45.520
The temperature has dropped just as predicted.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:47.230
Yeah.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:50.910
It's getting cold.

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:56.660
I don't think Takagi-san will lie to me.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:59.480
Then she'll have to admit it, right?

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.730
If I admit it, what will you do?

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:14.400
Will you come and warm me up?

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:21.130
You will warm me up, right?

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.060
No, I...

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.660
No, um...

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.900
Forget I said that.

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:31.660
Oh?

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:34.360
I give up! I give up!

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:39.560
Nishikata, you're really not good at this.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:44.960
So,

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:48.130
I win, right?

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:50.600
As a punishment, please come and warm me up.

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:51.300
What?

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:52.530
I'm kidding.

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:54.520
Seriously, Takagi-san!

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:57.000
Good morning.

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:03.500
Good... Good morning.

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:06.760
WINTER UNIFORM

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:07.660
Winter uniform.

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:11.900
So,

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:15.460
what happened to "wearing our winter uniforms together"?

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:18.480
Mina, did you send the message to Sanae?

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:21.060
I did.

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:22.140
Look.

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:22.840
SANAE-CHAN -OKAY -BYE-BYE.

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:23.720
LET'S WEAR OUR WINTER UNIFORMS TOMORROW.
NOT DELIVERED

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:26.630
The message was not delivered...

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:32.230
I'm really sorry.

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:35.200
Why was it not delivered?

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.830
Think about it the other way round.

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:46.000
Today is hot and sunny, right?

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:48.860
It's correct not to change into winter uniform.

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:52.230
I even want to roll up my sleeves.

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:54.700
I'm rolling them up now.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:01.500
Thank goodness it's hot today.

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:04.930
That's stupid...

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:06.230
Don't worry about it.

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:07.930
CREATING AN OPTIMISTIC, HEALTHY,
AND COMPETITIVE HIGH SCHOOL ENVIRONMENT

00:07:07.930 --> 00:07:09.100
See you.

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:17.060
I'm cold.

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:18.660
Sanae-chan.

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:23.260
I'm cold as well. Can I pull down my sleeves?

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:26.600
I'm sorry.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:36.620
Yes! It's finally time for lunch!

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:39.730
Have you brought your lunch box, Kimura?

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:44.040
He's absent because of food poisoning.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:45.230
Takao?

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:49.200
He's also absent because a game is released today.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:50.330
Sakurai?

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:52.930
He has a fever.

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:57.400
There are times when I have to eat alone.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:58.830
I heard something like that.

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:00.260
That's right.

00:08:10.060 --> 00:08:11.000
LUNCHBOX

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:12.020
Lunchbox

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:17.560
Sometimes, it's nice to eat alone.

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:20.660
I can enjoy the scenery through the window.

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:21.760
And more importantly,

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:24.930
there's fried chicken, the best side dish! That's right!

00:08:39.110 --> 00:08:41.330
It's still kind of lonely.

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:42.980
I found you.

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:46.160
Is it okay if I join you?

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:48.300
Okay.

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:50.660
But why?

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:54.030
That's because you seem alone today.

00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:58.030
I thought you might be lonely.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:01.100
So, I come to tease you.

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:04.660
You came to tease me because I'm lonely?

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:05.760
Don't you think that's weird?

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:07.600
Let's eat!

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:24.130
Your fried chicken looks delicious.

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:27.460
Do you want to bet on it?

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:29.760
She's going to challenge me again.

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:32.260
So, if I win,

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:34.730
I get your lotus roots.

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:36.900
Fried lotus roots. Okay.

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:40.230
The meat is the soul of every lunchbox.

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:43.630
I must not lose...

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:45.330
So,

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:48.160
what's the filling inside this rice ball?

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:51.130
It looks simple but I don't have the answer.

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:52.730
That's typical Takagi-san.

00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:56.360
Can I deduce from her other side dishes?

00:09:56.830 --> 00:09:58.960
No, that's difficult too.

00:09:59.460 --> 00:10:00.400
Should I just guess?

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:02.700
No, she will get my friend chicken if I lose.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.560
The risk is too high.

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:08.060
What should I do?

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:14.900
The answer is salmon.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:18.900
Okay, let's check the answer.

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:24.030
Takagi-san, I didn't see wrong.

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:25.830
I can see some of the salmon filling

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:28.530
exposed from that rice ball.

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:32.300
Your fried lotus roots are going to be mine.

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:38.000
The correct answer

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:42.030
is pickled plum.

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:43.530
What...

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:46.330
Thank you for the fried chicken.

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:49.930
That's right! Such a delicate lunchbox

00:10:49.930 --> 00:10:53.730
wouldn't have two rice balls with the same fillings.

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:57.780
My fried chicken!

00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:02.530
That's so sad.

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:06.760
In exchange, you can have my fried lotus roots.

00:11:07.530 --> 00:11:08.730
Is that all right?

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:09.300
Yeah.

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:11.360
But I lost.

00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:15.900
So, let's play a penalty game instead.

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:19.560
A penalty game?

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:29.740
Could the penalty be...

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:32.900
She's going to feed me directly?

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:44.980
What should we do for the penalty game?

00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:49.300
Eh? Could it be...

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:51.860
Do you want me to feed you?

00:11:53.860 --> 00:11:55.600
I was not thinking about that!

00:11:55.600 --> 00:11:56.700
Really?

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:57.860
I wasn't!

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:00.980
Seriously, Takagi-san!

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:05.160
That was fun.

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:06.580
Yeah, that's great.

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:08.660
But...

00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:12.400
It's better than eating alone.

00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:14.560
Thank you.

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:18.400
So, can I have lunch with you again?

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:27.280
Next time, I'm going to feed you just as you wanted.

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:29.080
I said I didn't want it!

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:36.440
Look! It's a photo of the UFO I've seen yesterday!

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:38.800
UFO!

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:43.880
It looks fake. Are you sure it's not some sort of bug?

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:45.390
It's real!

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:48.340
There was a strong flash yesterday night.

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:50.700
I turned back and saw the UFO!

00:12:50.840 --> 00:12:53.180
I took out my camera immediately,

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:55.190
and...

00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:58.120
It disappeared!

00:12:58.120 --> 00:12:59.040
Takao-kun.

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:02.780
Do you still believe in UFOs?

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:06.040
Don't look at me like that, Hibino!

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:08.780
Takao, what makes you think it's alright to talk like that?

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:11.180
I'm sorry...

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:12.320
That said,

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:14.980
You took a photo of something shiny
you threw into the fields, right?

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:16.240
You tried many times.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:19.600
What are you talking about?

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:21.630
I saw it. I was jogging back then.

00:13:29.900 --> 00:13:31.840
You should have greeted me at that time.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:34.260
I didn't want to. I felt disgusted.

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:48.380
It's a normal rock.

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:50.240
What are you doing?

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:53.160
I'm thinking if I can make it look like a UFO.

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:56.750
It's because of Takao-kun during lunch break, right?

00:13:57.260 --> 00:13:59.210
UFO is romantic, isn't it?

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:03.580
Let me help you.

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:08.420
Ready?

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:09.300
Okay!

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:14.060
It didn't work.

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:16.260
It looks just like a normal rock.

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:18.440
Is it too slow?

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:20.340
Anyway, let's try again.

00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:21.640
Okay.

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:27.370
Hey, Nishikata.

00:14:29.620 --> 00:14:30.240
What?

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:32.680
Do you believe in UFOs?

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:34.920
Of course.

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:39.630
Why are you laughing?

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:40.940
I'm sorry.

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:43.590
That's because you said it with a straight face.

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:47.860
Please toss it again.

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:55.220
No? Should I try it with a smaller rock?

00:14:58.020 --> 00:15:00.640
Do you believe in UFOs?

00:15:01.320 --> 00:15:04.500
Hmm... Not really.

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:06.380
I think it's a hoax.

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:09.920
That's not romantic at all.

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:11.360
Romance...

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:14.280
You don't like it?

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:17.670
No, I think it's all right.

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:23.700
Can you please throw again?

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:29.520
It doesn't feel right.

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:31.060
You're quite picky, aren't you?

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:33.600
But, since it's a romance,

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:35.560
shouldn't you aim to shoot a real UFO?

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:38.160
If it really appears, of course.

00:15:38.300 --> 00:15:40.120
But it doesn't.

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:45.180
If I'm an alien,

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:47.760
I wouldn't appear in front of you.

00:15:48.980 --> 00:15:50.300
I don't want to cause a ruckus.

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:53.400
But, if it's to tease you,

00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:55.720
it might be fun to show up once in a while.

00:15:55.900 --> 00:15:56.660
Daccha!

00:16:00.300 --> 00:16:01.880
If I'm an alien,

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:05.200
I will definitely capture people like you
who don't believe in aliens

00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:07.180
and scare you to death.

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:08.720
That's all right.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:11.600
It's fine to be captured if it's you.

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:19.400
You probably didn't capture that.

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:22.980
This is perfect! Look!

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:26.180
Eh?

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:29.780
That's amazing. It's just like the real thing!

00:16:30.220 --> 00:16:32.520
I'm going to post it and stir up the internet.

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:34.260
I will become famous!

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:37.900
What's wrong, Takagi-san.

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:44.960
Nishikata, that might be the real thing.

00:16:45.140 --> 00:16:48.260
It's just like the real thing!

00:16:48.660 --> 00:16:50.120
It's amazing!

00:16:50.930 --> 00:16:52.560
NIGHT

00:16:52.560 --> 00:16:53.160
Night.

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:56.850
MAME'S BATHHOUSE

00:17:05.780 --> 00:17:07.900
FEMALE

00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:10.990
MALE

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:16.620
Eh? That's weird.

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:19.540
A FEW HOURS AGO

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:21.540
You're going to the public bathhouse today?

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:24.540
Yeah, it's because my bathtub broke.

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:25.800
I see.

00:17:28.260 --> 00:17:29.600
When are you going?

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:32.200
Around 7 pm I think.

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:36.320
I see.

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:38.740
I thought

00:17:38.880 --> 00:17:41.360
she is going to be here since she said that.

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:56.880
It feels kind of disappointing...

00:18:01.060 --> 00:18:03.220
Or maybe lonely...

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:09.200
No, what am I thinking?

00:18:09.320 --> 00:18:10.240
There's no such thing.

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:12.220
I should feel relieved that she's not teasing me.

00:18:12.470 --> 00:18:13.930
PLEASE BUY ONE ITEM AT A TIME
CHANGE REFUND

00:18:14.220 --> 00:18:17.020
Right. Let me calm down
after drinking a bottle of fruit milk.

00:18:17.890 --> 00:18:18.350
BUY

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:21.220
Eh, it turns out you like fruit milk?

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:24.980
I want some coffee milk.

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:27.140
You came.

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:28.860
Why?

00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:31.760
Nothing... I thought you won't come.

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:35.560
Did you look for me?

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:38.760
Wha... No... I didn't!

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:41.720
That's because I need longer time to bathe.

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:44.760
So, I deduced the time when you will finish bathing

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:46.500
and went in earlier.

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:48.360
I'm quite accurate about it.

00:18:49.780 --> 00:18:52.200
Tsk! I feel as if I've lost!

00:19:05.720 --> 00:19:08.960
Takagi-san smells like soap.

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:15.180
Isn't this new to us?

00:19:16.280 --> 00:19:18.480
Walking together like this at night.

00:19:20.660 --> 00:19:21.620
Yeah.

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:24.720
We can't even see our faces properly.

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:30.380
Takagi-san, do you want to compete?

00:19:30.780 --> 00:19:32.460
Sure, what is it?

00:19:33.220 --> 00:19:36.020
Whoever blushes loses.

00:19:38.600 --> 00:19:39.900
What will you do, Takagi-san?

00:19:40.140 --> 00:19:42.480
As you can't check each other's faces in the dark,

00:19:42.480 --> 00:19:44.860
you can only lose by admitting your defeat.

00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:47.260
I can force it into a tie.

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:51.240
Sure, but you cannot admit you're blushing

00:19:52.320 --> 00:19:55.720
because you can't tell if you're blushing.

00:19:56.400 --> 00:19:57.400
That's right.

00:19:57.860 --> 00:19:59.440
So, what should we do?

00:20:01.740 --> 00:20:05.020
Though it's dark, we can see it if we are close enough.

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:09.080
Eh? You're blushing already.

00:20:10.460 --> 00:20:11.780
Did I win?

00:20:11.780 --> 00:20:15.260
No, we haven't started yet.

00:20:15.260 --> 00:20:17.010
Seriously, Takagi-san!

00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:20.120
How can I not blush if our faces are so close together?

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:21.000
That's despicable!

00:20:22.300 --> 00:20:23.760
So, should we start?

00:20:24.020 --> 00:20:25.340
Let's just forget it!

00:20:25.340 --> 00:20:27.340
I think I have bathed too long.

00:20:28.300 --> 00:20:30.980
But it's been quite a while now.

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:33.880
Can I check again?

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:35.220
No!

00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:45.420
That's fun.

00:20:45.820 --> 00:20:48.460
That tease was a hard one.

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:50.920
All right. I'm going this way.

00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:52.060
Takagi-san.

00:20:55.200 --> 00:20:56.640
Let me walk you home. It's dark.

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:14.980
Eh? What's with this pause?

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:17.780
Did I say something weird?

00:21:18.820 --> 00:21:21.260
It's too dark so I can't see her face.

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:29.680
It sounds like something you would say to your girlfriend.

00:21:32.380 --> 00:21:34.580
Really? No, I'm just...

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:36.660
It's not that far so it's all right.

00:21:37.220 --> 00:21:37.940
Thank you.

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:46.580
I think I've bathed for too long as well.

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:49.700
Never mind.

00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:52.420
Remember not to catch a cold.

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:56.580
Nishikata! You're blushing!

00:21:59.100 --> 00:22:01.120
No! I said I'd bathed too long...

00:22:01.120 --> 00:22:04.080
No! You didn't see it at all, did you?
